WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:126000

00:00.083 --> 00:02.750
-Have you ever lost someone close?
-My brother.

00:02.833 --> 00:05.291
And my husband. Celeborn.

00:05.375 --> 00:07.125
[Durin IV]
There's something under the mines.

00:07.208 --> 00:08.583
Ancient and powerful.

00:09.833 --> 00:10.791
[yells]

00:13.000 --> 00:15.875
[Disa] Your father's passing
has left us in a tangle.

00:15.958 --> 00:19.041
The Lords of the Blue Mountains
paid him vast tributes.

00:19.125 --> 00:20.708
They're demanding to collect.

00:20.791 --> 00:23.125
But there's more.
You are not your father's preferred heir.

00:23.208 --> 00:25.750
Your brother seems to be
gathering support.

00:26.708 --> 00:29.291
[Arondir] Theo. Lord of Pelargir.

00:29.375 --> 00:33.625
[Kemen] Pelargir is no longer a colony of
Númenor, but a fortress for its soldiers.

00:33.708 --> 00:35.125
And I am its Commander.

00:35.208 --> 00:37.083
We'll deliver
a regular allotment of timber

00:37.166 --> 00:40.083
for the construction of
His Majesty's armada.

00:40.583 --> 00:42.958
[Celebrimbor] Nine Rings to enslave
the world of Men.

00:43.041 --> 00:45.666
As he… enslaved me.

00:45.916 --> 00:47.750
-[yells]
-[grunts]

00:48.500 --> 00:50.333
[Sauron] Tell me where
you have hidden the Rings.

00:50.416 --> 00:52.125
And I will end your suffering now.

00:52.208 --> 00:54.000
[Celebrimbor] The Rings are
beyond your reach.

00:54.083 --> 00:56.041
As I shall be, ere long.

00:56.750 --> 00:59.000
[Elrond] That is the full record
of Celebrimbor's works.

00:59.083 --> 01:01.500
The wisdom of all
who ever dwelt in this place.

01:03.125 --> 01:03.958
[yells]

01:05.083 --> 01:07.708
I would have placed a crown
upon your head.

01:10.666 --> 01:12.291
The Rings are mine.

01:12.375 --> 01:15.458
[Gil-galad] Sauron's armies
are roving across Eriador.

01:15.541 --> 01:18.750
All Middle-earth is within his reach now.
Even Lindon.

01:18.833 --> 01:20.916
-[Galadriel] What is this place?
-[Elrond] A sanctuary.

01:21.000 --> 01:23.041
Protected… by the Elven Rings.

01:31.666 --> 01:35.875
[Galadriel] The war of the
Elves and Sauron is in its fifth year.

01:37.291 --> 01:41.125
Sauron has marched his armies
across the whole of Middle-earth…

01:41.625 --> 01:44.208
…conquering all in his path.

01:44.291 --> 01:46.750
Nothing can stop his advance,

01:47.375 --> 01:51.333
except the three Elven Rings,

01:52.125 --> 01:55.375
forged without Sauron's touch.

01:55.458 --> 01:59.125
In their powers of protection and healing,

01:59.208 --> 02:01.750
two Elven realms endure,

02:02.291 --> 02:04.000
Lindon and Rivendell…

02:05.000 --> 02:07.166
…fighting to hold back the shadow.

02:08.166 --> 02:11.083
But Sauron has Rings of his own.

02:11.583 --> 02:15.625
Seven for Dwarves, who so far
have resisted his influence.

02:15.708 --> 02:17.500
And nine for mortal Men…

02:17.875 --> 02:20.666
…who fall so easily to his will.

02:21.291 --> 02:24.083
But the two most
powerful kingdoms of Men…

02:24.458 --> 02:26.875
…have yet to declare a side.

02:26.958 --> 02:29.958
Mighty Númenor across the sea

02:30.041 --> 02:33.666
and Rhûn,
the vast desert power of the East.

02:34.666 --> 02:37.666
And it is whispered that
in the land of Mordor,

02:37.750 --> 02:40.250
the Dark Lord toils without rest…

02:41.000 --> 02:45.083
…obsessed with harnessing a power
to complete his conquest

02:45.166 --> 02:47.041
and rule them all.

02:48.916 --> 02:50.791
[dramatic music playing]

03:02.208 --> 03:03.416
[snarling]

03:04.041 --> 03:05.791
Hail Sauron!

03:06.500 --> 03:08.333
[all exclaiming] Hail Sauron!

03:12.166 --> 03:13.125
[grunting]

03:27.500 --> 03:28.500
[hissing]

03:47.916 --> 03:50.750
[in Black Speech]
One Ring to rule them all.

03:50.833 --> 03:55.333
Three Rings for the Elven-kings
under the sky.

03:55.416 --> 04:00.458
Seven for the Dwarf-lords
in their halls of stone.

04:00.541 --> 04:03.250
Nine for men doomed to die.

04:50.500 --> 04:51.791
[snarling]

05:01.666 --> 05:02.500
[grunts]

05:26.083 --> 05:27.583
[whimpering]

05:39.750 --> 05:40.583
[laughing]

05:47.458 --> 05:48.666
[all laughing]

05:52.750 --> 05:53.791
[shrieking]

06:03.541 --> 06:04.833
[shrieking]

06:15.125 --> 06:16.166
[snarling]

07:02.458 --> 07:04.666
[in English] All creation
requires sacrifice.

07:10.416 --> 07:12.625
Celebrimbor's secrets still elude us.

07:16.458 --> 07:20.875
I want the Elven Rings!

07:23.458 --> 07:25.291
Even one will suffice.

07:25.416 --> 07:26.791
[Orcs snarling]

07:27.958 --> 07:29.458
Expand the search.

07:30.416 --> 07:33.583
Any Elf who ever met Celebrimbor
is to be interrogated.

07:33.666 --> 07:36.250
Every record of his methods studied.

07:37.250 --> 07:38.583
Beg pardon, my lord…

07:40.291 --> 07:45.291
but when Eregion fell,
we put them records to the torch.

07:46.791 --> 07:48.166
On your orders.

07:50.625 --> 07:53.708
I also ordered you
to bring me the Elven-smiths.

07:53.791 --> 07:55.416
The Elven-smiths is dead.

07:57.041 --> 08:00.041
All of 'em now confirmed and counted for.

08:02.041 --> 08:05.041
Do you reckon… mayhap…

08:05.125 --> 08:08.958
Celebrimbor's secrets
died with him after all?

08:12.041 --> 08:13.666
What is your name, Orc?

08:16.000 --> 08:19.083
Marnûkh… my lord.

08:19.166 --> 08:20.500
Marnûkh.

08:25.208 --> 08:28.958
The answers we seek are out there…

08:30.416 --> 08:33.083
somewhere… waiting.

08:34.833 --> 08:38.750
The Orc who finds them
and brings them to me

08:40.041 --> 08:42.125
will be celebrated as a savior.

08:44.166 --> 08:46.166
He'll be the Orc who won the war.

08:47.250 --> 08:50.583
The Orc who won all wars.

09:03.500 --> 09:05.500
Don't you worry none, my lord.

09:06.208 --> 09:08.541
I'll… I'll find a way.

09:09.416 --> 09:10.916
You heard him!

09:11.583 --> 09:15.333
Come on, you lot! Move!

09:15.625 --> 09:17.750
[all exclaiming]

09:26.500 --> 09:29.041
[music intensifies]

10:02.916 --> 10:04.791
[birds chirping]

10:41.916 --> 10:43.250
[speaking indistinctly]

10:54.250 --> 10:55.291
[snarling]

11:08.416 --> 11:09.416
[sighs]

11:30.041 --> 11:31.041
Captain.

11:33.458 --> 11:35.166
It's an honor to see you, my lord.

12:21.541 --> 12:23.625
It isn't polite to stare.

12:24.958 --> 12:26.333
[Celeborn] I wasn't staring.

12:27.666 --> 12:29.333
Then what were you doing?

12:31.625 --> 12:33.000
Taking the air.

12:36.916 --> 12:41.000
Strange… to make war in such a place,
don't you think?

12:41.083 --> 12:42.791
Stranger still to celebrate it.

12:45.541 --> 12:47.041
Is that why you dance alone?

12:47.583 --> 12:49.041
I wasn't dancing.

12:50.750 --> 12:52.166
I was sparring.

12:53.666 --> 12:55.875
Don't you suppose
everyone would be better with the sword

12:55.958 --> 12:58.083
if they sparred with somebody else?

12:58.166 --> 13:00.083
I'm splendid with the sword.

13:00.166 --> 13:02.625
Well, as it turns out,
I'm not so terrible a dancer.

13:05.000 --> 13:06.458
What is your name?

13:16.416 --> 13:20.666
Touch flesh first… and I'll tell you.

13:21.125 --> 13:22.208
[chuckling]

13:37.791 --> 13:38.750
[grunts]

13:52.333 --> 13:53.375
[chuckling]

14:15.291 --> 14:16.208
[panting]

14:19.291 --> 14:20.750
You missed me.

14:43.750 --> 14:45.208
[dramatic music playing]

15:02.333 --> 15:03.666
Keep it.

15:05.916 --> 15:07.541
Celeborn.

15:11.166 --> 15:12.666
Galadriel.

16:11.791 --> 16:13.583
[Celeborn] I want to live here with you.

16:16.291 --> 16:17.791
This soil is exquisite…

16:20.250 --> 16:22.375
and the rest we'd need but time to shape.

16:25.083 --> 16:27.083
A spiral stair around every tree…

16:27.916 --> 16:28.750
[Galadriel] Hmm.

16:29.916 --> 16:32.333
…leading up to trellised homes
at the top.

16:35.875 --> 16:38.500
Bowers of mallorn limbs draped in silk.

16:42.375 --> 16:45.583
Fields of wildflowers so thick
they look like seas of colored glass.

16:48.583 --> 16:50.458
But what of the war?

16:52.875 --> 16:54.375
Wars will come and go.

17:00.375 --> 17:01.583
But this place here…

17:05.791 --> 17:07.416
It could be for always.

17:08.625 --> 17:13.458
Always… is a long time.

17:15.208 --> 17:16.625
Will you marry me?

17:20.333 --> 17:21.666
Yes.

17:23.458 --> 17:24.625
Yes.

17:24.708 --> 17:26.333
I will.

17:29.083 --> 17:30.541
[grunting]

17:37.416 --> 17:38.333
[groans]

17:40.041 --> 17:41.000
[grunts]

17:50.250 --> 17:51.250
[exclaiming]

17:54.250 --> 17:55.250
[grunting]

17:58.916 --> 17:59.875
[growling]

18:03.458 --> 18:04.333
[shouting]

18:06.500 --> 18:07.416
[gasping]

18:24.375 --> 18:25.375
[groaning]

18:34.583 --> 18:36.000
Lady Galadriel!

18:37.125 --> 18:39.750
[panting] They're falling back.
Should we pursue?

18:54.875 --> 18:55.958
Reform the line.

18:58.375 --> 18:59.500
[in Sindarin] REFORM THE LINE!

19:08.833 --> 19:10.083
CLOSE RANKS!

19:12.291 --> 19:13.500
HOLD FIRM!

19:25.333 --> 19:26.625
[all shouting]

19:35.541 --> 19:36.458
[grunting]

19:40.625 --> 19:42.375
[indistinct shouting]

20:02.083 --> 20:03.083
[grunting]

20:10.208 --> 20:11.416
[breathing heavily]

20:21.958 --> 20:24.000
[somber music playing]

20:46.625 --> 20:48.541
[in Sindarin] RING-SERVANT OF SAURON!

20:51.291 --> 20:53.000
[clamoring]

20:56.250 --> 20:57.375
[growling]

21:02.333 --> 21:03.666
[in English] Get everyone out of here!

21:07.291 --> 21:08.708
[in Sindarin] FALL BACK!

21:22.208 --> 21:23.583
[grunting]

21:30.125 --> 21:31.416
[horse snorting]

21:33.416 --> 21:34.875
[neighing]

22:07.833 --> 22:08.958
[neighing]

22:21.125 --> 22:22.583
[breathing heavily]

22:33.541 --> 22:36.833
[thumping]

22:44.916 --> 22:45.791
[straining]

22:50.041 --> 22:54.833
[Lossoth Nazgnagôl]
Your Ring belongs to Lord Sauron.

22:58.333 --> 22:59.541
Give it to me.

23:10.750 --> 23:11.750
[groaning]

23:17.208 --> 23:18.250
[grunting]

23:36.083 --> 23:37.208
[grunting]

23:37.500 --> 23:38.625
[breathing heavily]

23:59.583 --> 24:01.416
[music crescendos]

24:17.083 --> 24:19.083
The rest of 'em have gone, too.

24:19.166 --> 24:22.208
Some Elf trickery
covers their retreat, my lord.

24:23.458 --> 24:25.416
[Lossoth Nazgnagôl] Patience.

24:25.500 --> 24:30.458
The Elven Rings will not protect them
much longer.

24:30.958 --> 24:32.041
[clinking]

25:01.583 --> 25:06.625
Holding a hammer from Valinor
cannot make you Celebrimbor.

25:11.250 --> 25:13.416
You took part in the forging of the Seven…

25:14.750 --> 25:16.708
and of the Nine.

25:18.375 --> 25:22.375
But the Three… you had no hand in.

25:24.375 --> 25:25.875
Without knowing their secrets,

25:25.958 --> 25:28.791
you will never forge a Ring
capable of mastering them.

25:31.083 --> 25:32.791
Of mastering her.

25:35.125 --> 25:37.375
How does that feel?

25:38.958 --> 25:42.000
Knowing that the conquests
that you so desire

25:43.333 --> 25:45.750
shall forever elude your grasp.

25:51.000 --> 25:52.125
You held back from me.

25:54.458 --> 25:55.583
From your partner.

25:56.916 --> 25:58.208
[Celebrimbor] Partner?

25:59.458 --> 26:01.125
No, we were never partners.

26:03.208 --> 26:07.500
The machinery of your soul
is missing a piece.

26:09.041 --> 26:12.583
The one that allows for a true bond,
a true union with another being.

26:12.666 --> 26:16.041
So, in place of connection,
you seek control.

26:17.458 --> 26:19.500
But this is beyond yours.

26:20.916 --> 26:23.083
The work simply isn't in you.

26:25.041 --> 26:27.125
Even the Orcs have begun to realize it.

26:27.208 --> 26:31.166
Actually, I think
they're starting to pity you.

26:36.000 --> 26:37.625
[Shâgad] Lord Sauron…

26:39.375 --> 26:41.958
the delegation from Rhûn is arrived.

27:04.666 --> 27:07.708
The Dark Wizard accepts your alliance,
Lord Sauron.

27:08.333 --> 27:10.583
Rhûn and Mordor shall fight as one.

27:11.666 --> 27:13.583
How loyal are you to the Dark Wizard?

27:16.500 --> 27:20.166
It is said your ancestors ruled Rhûn
a thousand years before he arrived.

27:20.791 --> 27:23.833
When they refused to grant him
a place of honor in their court,

27:23.916 --> 27:27.000
he cursed their flesh
and that of their children's children.

27:27.083 --> 27:30.416
Do you really expect to gain our trust
by asking us to betray his?

27:30.625 --> 27:32.333
[snarling]

27:38.583 --> 27:39.875
[grunting]

27:43.833 --> 27:46.500
My proposed alliance
was never for your master.

27:52.583 --> 27:54.041
It was for you.

27:54.125 --> 27:56.041
For us? Why?

27:56.125 --> 27:58.375
Each of you is lord of a host of Horsemen.

27:59.166 --> 28:01.083
Ten thousand in number.

28:01.166 --> 28:03.041
Would you like to ride them
against the Elves?

28:04.250 --> 28:05.583
And the Dark Wizard?

28:06.416 --> 28:07.291
How are we supposed to…

28:07.375 --> 28:08.333
[grunting]

28:14.708 --> 28:16.583
Your people were once kings.

28:17.666 --> 28:21.625
Kings of the desert,
with power over millions.

28:23.625 --> 28:25.416
Would you like to be so again?

28:27.083 --> 28:28.750
[all] Yes, Lord Sauron.

28:33.166 --> 28:34.833
Under my instruction,

28:35.958 --> 28:39.625
nine Rings were forged for mortal Men.

28:46.250 --> 28:47.541
[snarling]

28:53.500 --> 28:55.916
Each bound with powers of sorcery…

28:57.333 --> 29:00.458
strength, the power to walk unseen…

29:02.250 --> 29:04.000
the power of life unending.

29:06.791 --> 29:08.166
This one I offer to you.

29:16.083 --> 29:17.291
[intense music playing]

29:31.208 --> 29:33.208
Rings of Power are precious gifts.

29:37.208 --> 29:38.833
I'm afraid Mordor…

29:43.791 --> 29:45.791
can share but one this day.

29:45.875 --> 29:48.458
[Third Gaudrim leader]
How are we to decide who bears it?

30:08.208 --> 30:09.208
[snarling]

30:20.916 --> 30:21.875
[yelling]

30:31.333 --> 30:32.625
[grunting]

31:03.458 --> 31:05.125
[bell tolling]

31:22.916 --> 31:24.000
[horse snorts]

31:25.583 --> 31:26.500
Arondir.

31:28.375 --> 31:29.333
[dog barking]

31:33.458 --> 31:34.750
Come here, come here.

31:43.000 --> 31:45.791
-Bind the wrist, two branches.
-Yes, two branches it is.

31:47.541 --> 31:48.583
[sighs]

31:51.958 --> 31:53.958
-Quickly.
-Now, drink some water.

32:02.875 --> 32:04.125
-Father!
-Father!

32:06.208 --> 32:07.083
You're here.

32:08.958 --> 32:11.708
Yes. I was afraid
I wouldn't see you again.

32:25.125 --> 32:26.541
That leg needs athelas root.

32:26.625 --> 32:27.625
Aye, my lord.

32:34.083 --> 32:35.166
Where are the others?

32:37.125 --> 32:37.958
[Elrond exhales]

32:53.458 --> 32:56.041
This new Nazgnagôl, who was he?

32:56.625 --> 32:58.958
I fear he may have been
King of the Lossoth.

33:00.958 --> 33:01.958
[softly] No.

33:03.250 --> 33:04.250
No.

33:06.583 --> 33:08.041
They pledged loyalty to us.

33:11.958 --> 33:14.416
And now he is a Ring-servant of Sauron.

33:16.750 --> 33:17.833
Just like the others.

33:20.541 --> 33:21.875
Just as well.

33:23.625 --> 33:25.083
We are safe here.

33:25.166 --> 33:27.541
And what of the world outside?

33:29.916 --> 33:33.208
Are we to close our doors
and watch as the forests burn?

33:33.291 --> 33:35.916
-We are doing all that we can.
-We could do more…

33:39.583 --> 33:42.958
if we had allies of our own.

33:45.041 --> 33:46.041
Galadriel.

33:48.208 --> 33:50.916
Míriel vowed that Númenor would return.

33:51.000 --> 33:53.125
Míriel no longer holds the Scepter.

33:53.208 --> 33:54.958
Then we appeal to her successor.

33:56.208 --> 34:00.166
No. We cannot put our hopes in Men.
It is clearly too dangerous.

34:00.250 --> 34:03.416
But the Men of Númenor are your kin.

34:03.500 --> 34:06.666
-Your brother's decision to--
-Elros does not enter into this.

34:12.125 --> 34:13.375
This is not my decision.

34:14.458 --> 34:16.958
It's the High King himself
who closed the door.

34:17.041 --> 34:21.541
He may reopen it
if you went to him and asked.

34:22.666 --> 34:24.500
My place is in Rivendell.

34:28.750 --> 34:30.250
I belong here.

34:41.125 --> 34:42.750
Sauron is close now.

34:45.833 --> 34:47.500
I can feel him.

34:50.875 --> 34:53.291
I can feel his very Eye upon my neck.

34:55.833 --> 34:58.250
He cannot reach you here, Galadriel.

35:01.375 --> 35:04.708
What haunts you now
is your own imaginings, nothing more.

35:06.333 --> 35:07.791
I have not seen Sauron in five years,

35:07.875 --> 35:10.250
not in the flesh
and certainly not in my mind.

35:12.291 --> 35:14.291
But I do know this.

35:15.250 --> 35:16.666
He will never stop.

35:19.833 --> 35:21.833
And we cannot defeat him alone.

35:51.500 --> 35:52.916
[Sauron] Galadriel.

35:53.458 --> 35:54.833
[breathing heavily]

35:58.541 --> 35:59.541
I see you.

36:02.250 --> 36:03.541
I know your mind.

36:08.958 --> 36:11.166
I would have placed a crown
upon your head.

36:14.500 --> 36:15.458
[sobbing]

36:17.708 --> 36:19.208
I would make you a queen.

36:23.500 --> 36:24.458
[gasping]

36:46.125 --> 36:47.208
You needn't worry.

36:48.750 --> 36:50.458
He will not be journeying far.

36:54.458 --> 36:55.833
Ill dreams?

36:58.833 --> 37:00.250
Why are you not abed?

37:02.750 --> 37:04.583
I might ask the same of you.

37:06.208 --> 37:07.833
Whenever I closed my eyes…

37:11.291 --> 37:13.833
I saw that boy's face, and I just…

37:17.666 --> 37:21.083
Why are secret pains so much easier
to escape in the daylight?

37:23.375 --> 37:24.583
What is yours?

37:26.916 --> 37:31.708
What happened out there today
was not your fault.

37:34.791 --> 37:36.791
You did not hand that boy a sword.

37:47.333 --> 37:48.708
But someone did.

37:52.375 --> 37:55.791
And had I not been neglectful in my duty
to the Men of Middle-earth…

37:57.833 --> 37:59.250
they might not have.

38:00.541 --> 38:01.958
You fear for Theo.

38:06.791 --> 38:07.833
[exhales]

38:08.958 --> 38:12.750
It has been an honor to serve with you,
Lady Galadriel.

38:14.416 --> 38:16.666
-But I must--
-Of course, Arondir.

38:18.500 --> 38:19.875
Go to Pelargir.

38:32.750 --> 38:34.333
[in Sindarin] Thank you…

38:36.833 --> 38:38.208
…my lady.

38:42.166 --> 38:44.041
[in English]
You never answered my question.

38:46.708 --> 38:49.000
Your secret pain?

38:51.250 --> 38:52.333
Loneliness.

39:19.250 --> 39:20.250
-Pick it up!
-[grunts]

39:23.416 --> 39:24.333
[soldier] Come on.

39:29.541 --> 39:32.000
[Kemen] Should have heard the wails
that tree-talker made

39:32.083 --> 39:34.083
when he saw we'd felled half a forest.

39:36.333 --> 39:38.083
Could hear him bellowing for miles.

39:39.125 --> 39:42.333
I trust you won't see my departure
as an excuse to slacken the reins.

39:43.541 --> 39:46.125
[Royal Númenórean soldier]
The work will continue unabated.

39:48.916 --> 39:50.583
I hope, for your sake, it does.

39:51.625 --> 39:54.791
My father's dealings in Middle-earth
are of supreme importance to him.

39:55.625 --> 39:57.250
That's why he sent me here.

39:57.916 --> 39:59.750
Armadas don't build themselves, you know.

40:00.791 --> 40:03.916
What of this summons
we received from Mordor?

40:04.791 --> 40:06.208
We are King's Men of Númenor.

40:08.750 --> 40:12.250
If any more of Mordor's slaveys come about
peddling magic jewelry,

40:12.333 --> 40:13.916
you're to slaughter them where they stand.

40:14.958 --> 40:16.375
Have I made myself clear?

40:16.958 --> 40:17.958
As cut glass.

40:21.083 --> 40:22.500
What a vile land.

40:25.041 --> 40:26.916
[male enforcer 2]
You'll stop when I tell you to stop!

40:27.000 --> 40:28.500
[male enforcer 1] More over there.

40:29.916 --> 40:32.125
-Pick up the pace.
-[man in Pelargir 4] What are you doing?

40:33.166 --> 40:35.375
-[male enforcer 3] Eyes down.
-[beaten man 2] Sorry, sir.

40:39.208 --> 40:40.625
[indistinct conversation]

40:48.000 --> 40:50.833
[Royal Númenórean soldier]
You there, slothabout.

40:52.166 --> 40:53.250
Twelve lashes.

41:03.625 --> 41:04.791
[grunting]

41:22.666 --> 41:24.375
[shudders]

41:28.500 --> 41:29.500
Your glove.

41:30.875 --> 41:31.875
Remove it.

41:36.750 --> 41:37.958
[shudders]

41:48.083 --> 41:49.375
[breathing heavily]

41:51.666 --> 41:52.791
Whom do you serve?

41:53.583 --> 41:57.875
I will die… for Sauron.

41:57.958 --> 41:59.208
No.

42:04.041 --> 42:05.875
You will live for him forever.

42:14.875 --> 42:15.916
[groaning]

42:19.333 --> 42:20.708
When wearing his Ring,

42:21.666 --> 42:25.041
a Nazgnagôl is both of this world
and of another.

42:25.291 --> 42:27.041
[grimacing]

42:27.166 --> 42:29.333
Your body is learning to dwell in both.

42:30.916 --> 42:32.375
The pain will pass.

42:33.666 --> 42:35.500
The power will not.

42:37.291 --> 42:38.625
Be grateful for it.

43:07.750 --> 43:09.083
[snarling]

43:24.791 --> 43:26.208
[whispering]

43:31.166 --> 43:33.083
[breathing heavily]

44:00.041 --> 44:02.458
What is your name, Easterling?

44:03.875 --> 44:04.875
Khamûl.

44:06.541 --> 44:07.541
Khamûl.

44:10.041 --> 44:11.416
Fairest of the Nine.

44:15.333 --> 44:16.750
We have work to do.

44:28.333 --> 44:29.625
[horse snorts]

45:02.791 --> 45:03.791
Durin.

45:05.875 --> 45:06.875
Elrond.

45:11.458 --> 45:12.458
There you go.

45:26.500 --> 45:28.666
Send your folk back in a few days.

45:29.500 --> 45:31.541
Narvi'll have eight more like it.

45:31.625 --> 45:33.250
You do too much, old friend.

45:35.541 --> 45:37.250
Well, not near enough, you ask me.

45:43.875 --> 45:45.208
We are managing, Durin.

45:45.291 --> 45:46.291
Aye.

45:47.000 --> 45:48.375
Managing to lose.

45:49.125 --> 45:52.083
I tell you, it's rank Dwarven pride

45:52.166 --> 45:54.625
to think that we can stay out
of this war forever, Elrond.

45:54.708 --> 45:56.333
Rushing into it would be no wiser.

45:59.208 --> 46:01.708
Durin, the Elves of the Greenwood report

46:01.791 --> 46:03.791
that your brother's en route
from the Iron Hills.

46:03.875 --> 46:06.500
I know. I'm not afraid of Thráin.

46:06.583 --> 46:08.500
He had two Dwarf-lords with him.

46:10.291 --> 46:12.458
Of sizable wealth,
judging by their banners.

46:13.833 --> 46:16.041
I fear he intends to contest your claim.

46:18.375 --> 46:23.416
Strange he'd contest it now, though,
with the war at such a tipping point.

46:23.500 --> 46:25.750
Gil-galad's offer
to formally back your kingship stands.

46:25.833 --> 46:28.500
No, no, no, no, no.

46:28.583 --> 46:30.625
You don't hire a fish to stoke a fire.

46:32.083 --> 46:35.333
No, this is a Dwarven matter.
It needs to stay that way.

46:37.958 --> 46:40.166
Am I the fish in this equation?

46:42.375 --> 46:43.375
Aye.

46:44.791 --> 46:46.791
The fish with the fairest hair.

46:47.625 --> 46:48.791
[both laughing]

46:51.250 --> 46:53.625
-Give my regards to Disa, won't you?
-Hmm.

46:54.708 --> 46:55.875
And the wee 'ns.

46:55.958 --> 46:57.083
Oh, not so wee anymore.

46:57.958 --> 47:00.166
Gerda just toasted her 17th. [sighs]

47:00.250 --> 47:01.666
-No.
-Aye.

47:03.333 --> 47:04.333
How?

47:08.041 --> 47:11.041
Time crawls
for Elves and mountains, Elrond.

47:13.041 --> 47:15.041
For the rest of us, it's bounding away.

47:18.000 --> 47:19.625
Then I shall return soon.

47:21.833 --> 47:23.541
-Stay longer next time.
-[Durin IV] Aye.

47:24.291 --> 47:26.458
And don't get your ears in a twist
about Thráin.

47:28.208 --> 47:29.875
I promise, we're ready.

47:31.583 --> 47:33.333
-[Gerda] No! Make it stop!
-[blowing horn]

47:33.416 --> 47:38.125
Aulë's arse, Gamli, it sounds like
you're murdering whatever poor goat

47:38.208 --> 47:39.416
you got that horn from.

47:39.500 --> 47:41.583
It's a ram's horn, Da.

47:41.666 --> 47:43.916
Well, ram it… somewhere else!

47:44.000 --> 47:46.958
Mum said I had to practice
for the welcoming ceremony.

47:47.041 --> 47:49.541
If you haven't learnt it by now,
your cousin Gila can play it.

47:49.625 --> 47:52.291
Has anybody seen the gold beard thread?

47:52.375 --> 47:54.958
Well, last I saw it,
it was by Aulë's shrine.

47:55.041 --> 47:56.250
Why does no one bother

47:56.333 --> 47:58.250
-to put things back?
-I smell something burning.

47:58.333 --> 47:59.791
Is there something burning back there?

47:59.875 --> 48:01.583
Who left it in here? It's all frayed--

48:01.666 --> 48:03.291
Uh, you said, "Well done."

48:03.375 --> 48:07.541
I said, "Don't put the bacon fat in
until after the ale cooks off."

48:07.625 --> 48:09.666
-I didn't!
-Same way you didn't hang

48:09.750 --> 48:12.291
-the washing over the fireplace.
-Put that thing down before I break it!

48:12.375 --> 48:14.416
-That wasn't my fault!
-You said I could play.

48:14.500 --> 48:17.166
Why does Gila get to? It's not fair!

48:17.250 --> 48:18.916
'Cause she won't bollocks it up.

48:19.791 --> 48:21.916
Honestly, the amount of headaches
that horn has given me…

48:22.000 --> 48:23.041
Don't fret!

48:25.125 --> 48:28.250
Just go finish getting dressed,
the pair of you.

48:32.416 --> 48:33.791
[footsteps receding]

48:39.916 --> 48:41.833
When did they get so grown?

48:42.041 --> 48:44.500
Ugh. I was thinking the same about us.

48:45.416 --> 48:47.875
This is the false stuff.
Where's the good thread?

48:47.958 --> 48:49.916
Agh. No one can tell the difference, love.

48:51.166 --> 48:53.416
Anyone who says they can is a liar.

48:53.500 --> 48:56.375
I just want you to look your best.

48:56.458 --> 48:59.583
As long as I have you by my side,
I look like a king.

49:01.250 --> 49:02.333
-Fasten me up.
-Hmm.

49:05.000 --> 49:05.833
Hmm.

49:06.625 --> 49:09.166
You haven't worn this one
since before we were married.

49:09.250 --> 49:10.416
-Haven't I?
-Mm…

49:10.500 --> 49:13.500
Well, it still fits. [groaning] Mostly.

49:15.541 --> 49:18.791
Look, let's both just take a breath.

49:20.375 --> 49:23.375
For all we know,
Thráin's just coming to pay his respects.

49:24.166 --> 49:26.166
With Blue-lords in tow.

49:26.250 --> 49:29.750
It's Rings that're on his mind,
not respects.

49:29.833 --> 49:31.583
[groaning] You've never liked Thráin.

49:31.666 --> 49:33.375
And you've always welcomed him
with open arms,

49:33.458 --> 49:35.791
no matter how many times
he blacks your eyes.

49:35.875 --> 49:37.000
He's my older brother, Disa.

49:38.583 --> 49:40.583
And he's all the family I've got left.

49:47.541 --> 49:48.833
Hmm.

49:52.166 --> 49:54.291
You need to be strong.

49:57.000 --> 49:58.000
I will be.

50:01.041 --> 50:05.083
[Narvi] My lords, ladies,
and distinguished guests…

50:05.583 --> 50:09.333
Khazad-dûm welcomes from the Iron Hills,

50:10.041 --> 50:13.125
Lord Balbur the Beardless.

50:15.833 --> 50:18.375
[horn blowing]

50:18.458 --> 50:21.000
[drums beating]

50:36.875 --> 50:39.083
And from the Blue Mountains,

50:39.166 --> 50:42.583
Lord Frór and Lady Freyja the Fair.

50:44.000 --> 50:46.541
[horn blowing]

51:00.375 --> 51:02.500
What a marvelous beard.

51:07.625 --> 51:09.041
That cannae be real, can it?

51:09.125 --> 51:10.750
She must have had it done.

51:11.625 --> 51:18.291
And returning to the halls of his birth,
Thráin, Prince of Khazad-dûm.

51:18.500 --> 51:20.791
[horn blowing]

51:30.875 --> 51:33.500
[indistinct whispering]

51:45.875 --> 51:47.125
What? What is it?

51:48.291 --> 51:49.291
What?

51:50.875 --> 51:53.375
[indistinct conversation]

52:09.083 --> 52:11.958
It seems he's fallen in
with some old friends

52:12.041 --> 52:13.750
and will be along shortly.

52:13.833 --> 52:17.833
Would you be so good, Delvemaster Narvi,
as to go and fetch him?

52:19.666 --> 52:20.666
Now.

52:33.750 --> 52:35.208
[all clamoring]

52:35.583 --> 52:36.875
Prince Thráin!

52:39.041 --> 52:40.375
Prince Thráin!

52:40.458 --> 52:41.666
The King respectfully--

52:41.750 --> 52:45.541
Tell my wee brother to ditch
the swan dance he's hosting and,

52:46.166 --> 52:48.583
and join us down here instead.

52:49.875 --> 52:53.000
For a celebration befitting a king!

52:53.125 --> 52:54.916
[all exclaiming]

52:56.250 --> 52:57.541
[burps]

53:03.375 --> 53:04.458
[Narvi]
Nearly there…

53:12.250 --> 53:14.666
Tell Thráin if he doesn't march

53:14.750 --> 53:16.708
his princely arse
to this hall this moment,

53:16.791 --> 53:20.250
I'll pluck his beard out, hair by hair,
and feed it to him!

53:20.416 --> 53:21.791
[breathing heavily]

53:21.958 --> 53:23.000
Come on.

53:23.958 --> 53:25.291
[panting]

53:25.416 --> 53:26.791
[all shouting]

53:28.583 --> 53:30.083
[Thráin] A princely arse?

53:31.708 --> 53:33.333
That's a princely arse!

53:34.000 --> 53:34.875
Eh?

53:36.083 --> 53:37.583
I'll give him more than that.

53:38.166 --> 53:39.625
[all exclaiming]

53:41.000 --> 53:42.416
[whimpering]

53:45.000 --> 53:48.208
Tell the Tavern-master,
by order of the King,

53:48.291 --> 53:50.208
all inns are hereby shut.

53:52.041 --> 53:56.375
And six ale barrels are to be brought
to the Great Hall at once!

53:56.458 --> 53:57.916
[female dwarf 1 in court] Only six?

53:58.333 --> 53:59.666
[male dwarf 1 in court coughing]

54:00.958 --> 54:03.916
Ten! Ten barrels of ale.

54:04.083 --> 54:05.541
[all cheering]

54:10.500 --> 54:13.541
Can someone else… tell him?

54:15.041 --> 54:16.791
[all laughing]

54:20.791 --> 54:22.875
-[Lord Frór] Thank you, my King!
-You're very welcome.

54:23.666 --> 54:25.125
[all laughing]

55:02.916 --> 55:05.291
[all cheering]

55:10.750 --> 55:13.208
Where are our Rings?

55:13.291 --> 55:16.500
The Seven Rings your father promised.
The Rings we paid for.

55:16.583 --> 55:20.541
We gave your father
half our mine yields for months.

55:20.625 --> 55:23.625
Sauron had a hand in their creation.

55:26.333 --> 55:30.416
It was over-digging caused by those Rings
led to my father's death.

55:30.500 --> 55:32.291
In a mining accident.

55:32.375 --> 55:35.541
Aye. A tragic one.

55:35.625 --> 55:38.166
Khazad-dûm will compensate you
for your losses,

55:39.416 --> 55:43.250
but the Rings have been hidden away
someplace, known only to the King.

55:44.166 --> 55:46.958
There to remain till we've
a means of destroying them.

55:47.041 --> 55:49.458
Destroyin' 'em? With Middle-earth at war?

55:49.541 --> 55:52.416
Elves bear Rings. Men bear Rings.

55:52.500 --> 55:54.958
-The Dwarves cannot be left behind.
-Aye!

55:55.041 --> 55:56.583
You dinnae' bring a dagger
to a dragon fight.

55:56.666 --> 55:59.375
"Pick 'em up, ya whelp-rats!"

56:02.208 --> 56:05.208
That's what our father used to say
when he'd find our toys in here.

56:06.625 --> 56:07.625
"Pick 'em up."

56:09.125 --> 56:11.791
And I'd always tell him,
"Durin left 'em out,"

56:12.875 --> 56:15.750
but somehow he always knew it was me.

56:16.791 --> 56:22.041
But not even as babes would
Durin or I have dared sully this hall

56:22.125 --> 56:25.125
with such mouncin' as you lot have today!

56:26.291 --> 56:28.666
Are you Dwarves or dogs?

56:31.833 --> 56:34.833
Your king has spoken.

56:39.500 --> 56:41.000
Now bow your heads.

56:52.000 --> 56:56.083
Guards, kindly see our guests
find their chambers.

57:00.875 --> 57:05.166
Might I be permitted a word
with my brother first?

57:11.083 --> 57:12.083
Tell me.

57:13.083 --> 57:14.416
None of that pish.

57:17.041 --> 57:18.791
What really happened to Father?

57:32.791 --> 57:34.416
I wish I could have seen it.

57:36.708 --> 57:38.666
When he made that leap.

57:41.833 --> 57:42.958
No, you don't.

57:44.458 --> 57:45.791
What'd you put in the casket?

57:48.000 --> 57:53.166
Cloak, axe and his favorite boots.

57:53.250 --> 57:54.958
The ones with the squeaky latch?

57:55.708 --> 57:56.750
Mm-hmm.

57:57.041 --> 57:58.041
I gave those to him.

57:59.416 --> 58:01.083
Why'd ya think I put 'em in?

58:06.000 --> 58:07.333
Your move.

58:18.791 --> 58:20.000
It's funny.

58:22.125 --> 58:23.958
I hadn't spoken to him in years,

58:25.625 --> 58:27.750
but as soon as I heard I couldn't anymore…

58:30.500 --> 58:31.833
it's all I wanted to do.

58:35.833 --> 58:37.458
[sighs] When they crowned me…

58:39.750 --> 58:40.708
[sighs]

58:41.083 --> 58:42.333
for a moment…

58:44.375 --> 58:46.750
I swear, I thought I could hear his voice.

58:48.500 --> 58:49.708
What'd he say?

58:52.208 --> 58:53.041
[scoffs]

58:53.500 --> 58:54.583
Tell me.

58:55.958 --> 58:56.833
[sighs]

59:01.958 --> 59:03.000
"I'm with you."

59:06.875 --> 59:08.541
You should've just told me.

59:09.208 --> 59:13.458
About Father, about the Rings, Durin.

59:14.291 --> 59:15.708
It's me.

59:17.958 --> 59:19.166
You can trust me.

59:25.750 --> 59:27.458
You can come out now, Disa.

59:28.958 --> 59:31.125
I didn't want to interrupt, is all.
[sighs]

59:32.083 --> 59:33.791
Bat wings! My favorite.

59:34.666 --> 59:37.875
Durin, Narvi's sent word.
He's waiting for you in the armory.

59:38.916 --> 59:40.250
Don't cheat while I'm out.

59:41.750 --> 59:43.250
Why cheat? I always win.

59:43.333 --> 59:44.916
'Cause you always cheat.

01:00:00.041 --> 01:00:01.041
Didi.

01:00:04.916 --> 01:00:07.333
Don't call me that. Ever.

01:00:08.458 --> 01:00:12.875
My husband might be blind to your pish,
but I'm not buyin' a drop of the stuff.

01:00:14.708 --> 01:00:16.375
What are you really doing here?

01:00:17.000 --> 01:00:21.750
What? Isn't visiting an old flame
reason enough?

01:00:22.333 --> 01:00:24.541
There was never a flame.

01:00:25.625 --> 01:00:27.458
And now there aren't even embers.

01:00:28.541 --> 01:00:29.625
Come on.

01:00:30.416 --> 01:00:32.250
It was so long ago.

01:00:32.333 --> 01:00:34.166
Can't we laugh about it now?

01:00:37.166 --> 01:00:39.708
There's nothing to laugh about.

01:00:42.000 --> 01:00:43.000
Mum?

01:00:44.708 --> 01:00:45.708
Gamli.

01:00:47.000 --> 01:00:50.708
Your Uncle Thráin was just saying
how well he thought you did today.

01:00:50.791 --> 01:00:53.291
Aye. Aye. You…

01:00:54.583 --> 01:00:57.250
You played that goat horn
like you were born with it.

01:00:58.291 --> 01:00:59.708
It's a ram's horn.

01:01:02.708 --> 01:01:05.000
Aye. Aye.

01:01:13.041 --> 01:01:15.833
Tell Elrond,
soon as he needs more, to send word.

01:01:16.250 --> 01:01:17.458
[horse neighing]

01:01:26.375 --> 01:01:28.916
How long you been runnin' swords?

01:01:30.416 --> 01:01:32.958
You shite weasel. You followed me.

01:01:33.041 --> 01:01:35.541
Be glad it was me and not the Blue-folk.

01:01:36.250 --> 01:01:39.000
If they found out you were supplying
the Elves in secret…

01:01:39.583 --> 01:01:41.500
You are after my throne, aren't you?

01:01:42.166 --> 01:01:44.333
-Aren't you?
-Durin, just calm down!

01:01:44.416 --> 01:01:45.250
[grunting]

01:01:45.416 --> 01:01:47.791
-You cave-crawling--
-Durin! Don't be daft!

01:01:48.666 --> 01:01:49.541
[screaming]

01:01:59.333 --> 01:02:00.416
[growling]

01:02:04.375 --> 01:02:08.333
I have knowledge
that could save Middle-earth.

01:02:25.041 --> 01:02:26.083
Did you see it?

01:02:30.666 --> 01:02:31.916
The Orc?

01:02:46.250 --> 01:02:49.333
[Gil-galad] Thousands of Orcs
bearing down on us for months.

01:02:49.416 --> 01:02:51.541
Now the Rings show us one.

01:02:52.666 --> 01:02:53.833
Why? What does it mean?

01:02:54.791 --> 01:02:56.000
It means that whoever he is,

01:02:56.083 --> 01:02:59.291
his actions will somehow
shape our fortunes in this war.

01:03:00.541 --> 01:03:02.625
But for good or ill, we cannot yet see.

01:03:04.875 --> 01:03:06.583
There's more, isn't there?

01:03:12.458 --> 01:03:14.958
We have fought Sauron to a stalemate.

01:03:15.041 --> 01:03:18.625
And now his Eye turns to Men
to bolster his ranks.

01:03:18.708 --> 01:03:23.583
Lossoth from the North,
Haradrim from the South.

01:03:28.208 --> 01:03:29.625
Where will he turn next?

01:03:32.666 --> 01:03:33.833
Rhûn.

01:03:36.500 --> 01:03:37.541
[clanking]

01:03:44.791 --> 01:03:48.625
Between the Dark Wizard's followers
and your Horsemen,

01:03:49.916 --> 01:03:51.833
how many can you bring to my banner?

01:03:52.791 --> 01:03:54.958
A hundred thousand, my lord.

01:04:00.083 --> 01:04:02.375
We could never hope
to withstand such a force.

01:04:03.666 --> 01:04:09.000
Then let us pray there is some other power
out there… that can.

01:04:28.625 --> 01:04:30.541
There is another wizard in Rhûn,

01:04:31.250 --> 01:04:33.750
one who opposes us at every turn.

01:04:33.833 --> 01:04:37.166
It is said his power comes
from the Secret Fire itself.

01:04:37.250 --> 01:04:38.250
Ride to Rhûn.

01:04:40.208 --> 01:04:41.916
I will see to Gandalf myself.

01:04:54.500 --> 01:05:00.083
Lord Sauron, another delegation
of mortal Men have arrived.

01:05:02.083 --> 01:05:03.250
Men of Númenor?

01:05:04.416 --> 01:05:05.625
No, my lord.

01:05:06.875 --> 01:05:13.625
If granted Rings, these Men promised
to lead a rebellion against Númenor.

01:05:42.416 --> 01:05:43.750
[Sauron] The Rings of Power…

01:05:45.041 --> 01:05:46.666
are precious gifts.

01:05:53.791 --> 01:05:56.208
Mordor can share but one this day.

01:06:21.750 --> 01:06:23.250
[both grunting]

01:06:37.833 --> 01:06:40.458
Now is the mighty hour come.

01:06:41.916 --> 01:06:43.000
Let the hunt begin.

01:06:44.375 --> 01:06:45.208
[gasps]

01:06:51.416 --> 01:06:54.208
[Marnûkh] The Dark Lord is on the brink
of craftin' a new power.

01:06:55.250 --> 01:06:56.458
What is preventing him?

01:06:56.541 --> 01:06:58.291
Celebrimbor's secrets.

01:07:00.416 --> 01:07:03.916
He's got armies scouring Middle-earth
to find the answer.

01:07:04.833 --> 01:07:05.916
I cannot trust an Orc.

01:07:06.000 --> 01:07:06.916
We have no choice.

01:07:07.000 --> 01:07:08.541
Then I shall go with you.

01:07:12.583 --> 01:07:16.333
[Khamûl] The Dark Lord summons
the armies of Rhûn to Middle-earth!

01:07:17.625 --> 01:07:19.458
Middle-earth will burn.

01:07:20.000 --> 01:07:23.208
That death might well be
the price of saving it.

01:07:25.208 --> 01:07:26.500
[Galadriel] Celeborn.

01:07:26.583 --> 01:07:27.791
[sobbing] Where were you?

01:07:28.666 --> 01:07:30.000
Trying to get back to you.

01:07:32.500 --> 01:07:33.875
[Gil-galad] The Elves will fall.

01:07:35.208 --> 01:07:37.583
His eye will turn to Númenor.

01:07:41.041 --> 01:07:45.250
[Lord Belzagar] If you can't make your own
subjects kneel, how can you make Sauron?

01:07:45.833 --> 01:07:46.833
[grunting]

01:07:49.833 --> 01:07:52.125
-Snuff out this rebellion.
-I am ready, Father.

01:07:52.583 --> 01:07:54.291
[both grunting]

01:08:00.666 --> 01:08:02.125
[Thráin] You made us weak,

01:08:03.833 --> 01:08:05.375
I'll make us strong.

01:08:07.041 --> 01:08:09.208
[Galadriel] A Master Ring
would give Sauron the power…

01:08:10.083 --> 01:08:11.416
to govern our minds.

01:08:12.041 --> 01:08:12.875
[whimpering]

01:08:14.583 --> 01:08:15.958
Come with me.

01:08:17.916 --> 01:08:22.208
You and I can see to it
Sauron never completes his Ring.

01:08:26.208 --> 01:08:28.041
The Dark Lord, we have to stop him.

01:08:31.375 --> 01:08:33.583
The shadow rises in Middle-earth.

01:08:37.250 --> 01:08:38.625
How would you like to rise with it?

01:08:43.500 --> 01:08:45.833
[closing theme music playing]
